This folder contains commands which establish invairants for the world state.

Example:
invariant [PRE|POST] <participant_name> <type> <arg_1>...<arg_n>

This establishes a pattern where an invariant type is applied to a participant
with the provided arguments. The PRE or POST arguments indicate if the invariant
is being evaluated before or after the world transformation.

The failure modes which determine behavioral semantic validity become:
- Missing required pre-transformation participant
- Pre-transformation invariant violation
- Invalid post-world state after transformation
- Post-transformation invariant violation
